DaRuntimeMcpTools: reuse and reclaim the process-wide runtime MCP registration

runtimeConfig.mcpServers are registered process-wide, keyed by fingerprint.

1. Reuse. mountServer() called addMcpServer() for every task and treated the
   core's "MCP server id already exists" as an unavailable server. DA builds a
   new agent per task (the resume after an ask_user answer is a new task too),
   so only the first task of a session could see the runtime MCP tools. When
   the add fails but the id is registered, mount the existing registration.

2. Reclaim. Registrations were never removed ("全局注册不随卸载回收"), so every
   distinct snapshot (e.g. one MCP address per team-member session) kept a
   registration and a live client until the process restarted. Count the agent
   views per server id; the last unmount unregisters it (which also
   disconnects the client).

Applied by deploy/compose/da/build.sh until fixed upstream (agent-solution common).

